  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset-level associations after this appraisal: H3 KEAP1 loss positive/validated (weaker dependency); H13 TP53 loss positive (weaker dependency); H26 SMARCA4 loss negative/validated (stronger dependency). Conditional robustness supports independence from co-loss patterns: H33 SMARCA4 in TP53-/KEAP1-intact +0.814; H37 KEAP1 in SMARCA4-intact +0.809; H38 TP53 in SMARCA4-intact +0.828. SMARCA4 robust in Avana and Ky libraries: H34/H35. These remain dataset associations, not causality or external generalization.\n\nCDKN2A is consistently near threshold but not above it: overall +0.139, TP53/KEAP1-intact +0.144, triple-intact +0.144. Not accepted; closed/inconclusive for now. H39 invalid due tiny cell. ARID1A, RB1, SMAD4, BRCA2 loss not supported.\n\nPTEN loss is a new borderline candidate: H44 signed +0.239 [0.145, 0.332], raw PTEN loss more negative dependency_composite (stronger dependency). Lower bound just below 0.15; multiple testing warrants caution. Requested independent validation of H44. Registered PTEN Avana, Ky, and TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact follow-ups. Do not accept PTEN unless validation or additional robustness evidence is sufficiently above threshold.",
