  "narrative": "The newly delivered validation and interaction tests substantially consolidate the current scientific picture as a set of supplied-dataset associations, not causal effects or externally generalizable biology. H108 is the most consequential new result. Among samples lacking TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, SMARCA4 loss, and MSI-high status, PTEN loss has signed estimates of +0.260 [0.182, 0.338] in discovery and +0.275 [0.154, 0.397] in independent validation. Both intervals exceed the 0.15 composite-unit threshold in the claimed stronger-dependency direction, with the validation lower bound only narrowly above threshold because the validation interval is intentionally stringent. I therefore accept and close H108 as the cleanest independent confirmation of the moderate PTEN association after removing the largest competing genomic effects. H82 is also resolved: MSI-high status among TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, SMARCA4-intact cells has discovery +0.745 [0.666, 0.825] and validation +0.779 [0.675, 0.884], both far above threshold; I accept and close H82, indicating that the MSI-high stronger-dependency association is not merely a consequence of co-occurring TP53, KEAP1, or SMARCA4 loss. The formal MSI-high by TP53-loss interaction in H88 is unsupported: the signed discovery estimate was -0.012 [-0.255, 0.231] and validation was -0.139 [-0.495, 0.217], with intervals crossing null and not exceeding the threshold in the registered negative-interaction direction. I reject and close H88. H55, the negative-signed SMARCA4 by adenocarcinoma interaction, is likewise unsupported: signed discovery estimate -0.174 [-0.312, -0.035] and validation estimate -0.084 [-0.281, 0.113]. Although a positive-sign counterpart was discovered in one analysis, its independent interval was not above threshold, so formal lineage-specific heterogeneity should not be claimed; direct SMARCA4 loss within adenocarcinoma remains supported as a subgroup mean difference. The broader supported supplied-dataset findings are now stable. TP53 loss is associated with weaker dependency, signed +0.829 [0.767, 0.891], and remains strong across batch_a, Avana, KY, adenocarcinoma, high screen quality, high Cas9 activity, and high aneuploidy. KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker dependency, signed main +0.810 [0.745, 0.875] and validated +0.788 [0.698, 0.879], also robust across batch_a, libraries, adenocarcinoma, screen quality, Cas9 activity, and high aneuploidy. SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger dependency, signed main +0.804 [0.742, 0.867] and validated +0.800 [0.705, 0.895], robust across libraries, adenocarcinoma, clean TP53/KEAP1 states, stemness extremes, high Cas9, elevated mutation burden, and high aneuploidy. MSI-high is associated with much stronger dependency, signed main +0.775 [0.664, 0.885] and validated +0.842 [0.673, 1.010], robust across triple-intact, adenocarcinoma, batch_a, Avana, screen quality, mutation burden, Cas9 activity, and high aneuploidy. PTEN loss is a moderate stronger-dependency predictor, main +0.239 [0.145, 0.332] and validated +0.279 [0.138, 0.419], and it is now well confirmed in the quadruple-intact clean stratum. Important negative or unsupported findings include STK11 loss, KRAS mutation, MYC amplification, MTAP loss, ARID1A loss, RB1 loss, SMAD4 loss, BRCA2 loss, PIK3CA mutation, APC mutation, NF1 loss, media serum percentage, and research markers D, E, and F; ERBB2 amplification and BRAF V600E are near-null; EGFR amplification does not support a stronger-dependency effect in the registered direction. Most formal interaction tests are negative, indicating that the accepted predictors are largely additive associations rather than evidence for multiplicative subgroup modification. Remaining uncertainty is mostly precision-limited rather than contradictory: PTEN remains less robust in some direct subgroups such as batch_a, KY, high aneuploidy pending direct testing, and triple-intact high-Cas9; CDKN2A is near threshold and still needs a clean quadruple-intact estimate; several adenocarcinoma amplifier and EMT or hypoxia strata remain untested. The most informative next analyses are the registered clean PTEN-adenocarcinoma refinement and CDKN2A quadruple-intact test, followed by direct PTEN checks in adenocarcinoma and high aneuploidy, Avana-library main-effect scale checks, and adenocarcinoma-specific amplifier associations. All conclusions should remain framed as associations in this supplied dataset, not as causal single-gene knockout effects or claims of external biological generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Supplied-dataset associations only. Accepted main predictors: TP53 loss weaker dependency, signed +0.829 [0.767,0.891]; KEAP1 loss weaker dependency, signed main +0.810 [0.745,0.875] validated +0.788 [0.698,0.879]; SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency, signed main +0.804 [0.742,0.867] validated +0.800 [0.705,0.895]; MSI-high stronger dependency, signed main +0.775 [0.664,0.885] validated +0.842 [0.673,1.010]; PTEN loss moderate stronger dependency, signed main +0.239 [0.145,0.332] validated +0.279 [0.138,0.419]. Robust strata include TP53/KEAP1 across batch_a, Avana, KY, adenocarcinoma, high screen quality, high Cas9, high aneuploidy; SMARCA4 across libraries, adenocarcinoma, clean TP53/KEAP1 states, stemness extremes, high Cas9, elevated mutation burden, high aneuploidy; MSI-high across triple-intact, adenocarcinoma, batch_a, Avana, screen quality, mutation burden, Cas9 activity, high aneuploidy. Newly accepted/closed: H108 PTEN quadruple-intact excluding TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4/MSI signed +0.260 [0.182,0.338] validated +0.275 [0.154,0.397], accept/close; H82 MSI triple-intact validated +0.779 [0.675,0.884], accept/close. Newly rejected/closed: H88 MSI by TP53 interaction, R71 -0.012 [-0.255,0.231], R107 -0.139 [-0.495,0.217]; H55 SMARCA4 by adenocarcinoma negative interaction, R48 -0.174 [-0.312,-0.035], R80 -0.084 [-0.281,0.113]; direct SMARCA4 adenocarcinoma association remains accepted, but formal interaction is not robust. Main accepted claims H3/H13/H26/H44 closed as completed validated robustness claims. Negative or unsupported: STK11, KRAS, MYC amplification, MTAP, ARID1A, RB1, SMAD4, BRCA2, PIK3CA, APC, NF1, media serum, research markers D/E/F, ERBB2, BRAF; EGFR unsupported in registered direction; Ky main positive library shift rejected -0.061 [-0.129,0.008]. Unresolved precision issues: PTEN batch_a, KY, screen-quality, triple-intact high-Cas9, high aneuploidy direct tests; CDKN2A near threshold pending clean estimate; adenocarcinoma amplifier and EMT/hypoxia strata untested. Next analyze priority: new H108 clean-stratum adenocarcinoma PTEN refinement, H118 CDKN2A quadruple-intact, H113 PTEN high aneuploidy, H50 PTEN adenocarcinoma, H117 Avana main effect, H104-H106 adenocarcinoma amplifier effects, H115/H116 EMT/hypoxia TP53/KEAP1 checks. Interpret all findings as supplied-dataset associations only, not causal or externally generalizable."
