  "narrative": "The new discovery results largely reinforce the robustness of the accepted large predictors and clarify which moderate or borderline associations remain precision-limited. In orthogonal biological stress states, TP53 loss remains associated with weaker dependency in high EMT (+0.832 [0.718, 0.946]), KEAP1 loss remains associated with weaker dependency in high hypoxia (+0.800 [0.677, 0.924]), SMARCA4 loss remains associated with stronger dependency in high EMT (+0.763 [0.634, 0.893]) and high hypoxia (+0.848 [0.725, 0.971]), and MSI-high remains associated with stronger dependency in high EMT (+0.610 [0.413, 0.808]). These intervals are entirely above the 0.15-unit threshold, so I accept and close these subgroup robustness checks. The MSI-high high-EMT estimate uses a small exposed cell, but even the 95% lower bound exceeds threshold, so the association is supported in this dataset.\n\nFor PTEN loss, the moderate stronger-dependency signal is again localized in a biologically clean adenocarcinoma stratum. After excluding TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, SMARCA4 loss, and MSI-high status, PTEN loss among adenocarcinomas has signed estimate +0.279 [0.186, 0.373], entirely above threshold. This is a meaningful refinement of the already validated general PTEN and clean-quadruple-intact PTEN associations, so I accept H119 and request validation as the most informative remaining PTEN claim. In contrast, direct high-aneuploidy PTEN (+0.271 [0.087, 0.455]), high-EMT PTEN (+0.328 [0.143, 0.513]), and high-hypoxia PTEN (+0.261 [0.087, 0.435]) have point estimates above threshold but lower bounds below threshold. I leave them unresolved and deferred rather than accepting them as independent evidence, because the uncertainty does not exclude differences smaller than the scientifically meaningful threshold.\n\nCDKN2A remains unresolved. In the quadruple-intact clean stratum, the signed estimate is +0.148 [0.093, 0.204], slightly below threshold; in the clean low-9p21 refinement it is +0.151 [0.090, 0.212], barely above threshold but with a lower bound below threshold. These results do not justify accepting CDKN2A as a meaningful predictor, but they are not clearly null, so I defer them. EGFR amplification within adenocarcinoma is not supported in the registered direction: signed estimate -0.027 [-0.149, 0.095], with an interval crossing both null and threshold, so I reject and close H104. All interpretations remain supplied-dataset associations, not causal knockout effects or externally generalizable biology.",
