  "research_notes": "Supplied-dataset associations only; no causal or generalizability claims. Updated final model: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss associate with weaker dependency; SMARCA4 loss, MSI-high, and PTEN loss associate with stronger dependency. PTEN effects are moderate but robust, including H44 overall validated, H49 clean quadruple-intact validated, H108 clean quadruple-intact plus MSI-intact validated, and H119 clean quadruple-intact adenocarcinoma validated. H159 is now independently validated: SMARCA4-loss stronger-dependency effect in clean adenocarcinoma excluding TP53/KEAP1/MSI is +0.792 discovery and +0.759 validation, decisive. H119 PTEN clean adenocarcinoma validated: +0.279 discovery, +0.289 validation, lower bound just above threshold but still decisive. Robustness across libraries, batch, quality filters, high/low aneuploidy main contexts, adenocarcinoma contexts, EMT/hypoxia contexts, fast doubling main contexts, and co-occurrence exclusions is extensive. Negative/unsupported claims include most interactions: TP53 x KEAP1, PTEN x co-occurring predictors, PTEN fast/slow clean interaction, MSI x TP53 validation, SMARCA4 subtype/stemness interactions, and many technical/context interactions. Negative predictors include STK11, KRAS, MYC, MTAP, ARID1A, RB1, SMAD4, BRCA2, PIK3CA, APC, NF1, media serum, global EGFR/ERBB2/BRAF checks, and research markers. Unresolved: CDKN2A borderline near threshold but lower bounds often below threshold; do not accept without decisive lower bound above 0.15. Some PTEN localization contexts remain unresolved or underpowered. Next priority: formal high-aneuploidy interaction tests for TP53, KEAP1, SMARCA4, MSI-high, and PTEN. If null, maintain additive interpretation. Validation budget is exhausted, so further refinement should rely on discovery precision and prespecified intervals."
}

