  "narrative": "The newly delivered evidence reinforces the working additive supplied-dataset association model and provides no decisive support for context modification. H146 and H147 are robust main-effect checks in the higher mutation-burden stratum. TP53 loss remains associated with weaker dependency: signed estimate +0.823 [0.735, 0.911]. KEAP1 loss similarly remains associated with weaker dependency: +0.783 [0.686, 0.880]. Both signed lower bounds are far above the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed direction, so both are accepted as within-dataset associations. They do not establish causal knockout effects, biological mechanism, or external generalizability; correlated lineage/subtype/co-perturbation/technical factors could still contribute.\n\nH50 tests PTEN loss within adenocarcinoma: signed estimate +0.227 [0.121, 0.333]. The point estimate is above 0.15 units and the interval excludes zero, but the lower bound falls below the effect-size threshold. It is consistent with the previously accepted broader and validated PTEN-loss stronger-dependency signal, but this adenocarcinoma-specific claim is not decisive enough to accept. I leave it unresolved and close it rather than overstate a subgroup-specific thresholded effect.\n\nThe ten delivered interaction tests, H172-H180, are all non-decisive for the pre-specified claimed contexts. For high-EMT contexts, H172 TP53 is +0.005 [-0.131, 0.140]; H173 KEAP1 is -0.100 [-0.249, 0.048], opposite to the claimed weaker-dependency amplification; H174 SMARCA4 is -0.053 [-0.200, 0.095]; H175 MSI-high is -0.218 [-0.452, 0.017]; and H176 clean PTEN is -0.053 [-0.243, 0.137]. For high-stemness contexts, H177 TP53 is +0.035 [-0.105, 0.175]; H178 KEAP1 is -0.066 [-0.219, 0.087]; H179 MSI-high is +0.043 [-0.217, 0.303]; and H180 PTEN is +0.103 [-0.099, 0.305]. In none of these is the signed lower bound decisively above 0.15 in the claimed interaction direction, and all intervals include zero. Many intervals are wide because interaction cells are small, and this follows many interaction tests without multiplicity adjustment.\n\nH175 deserves scrutiny because its signed point estimate has magnitude beyond 0.15 units but in the direction opposite the pre-specified stronger-dependency interaction, with interval [-0.452, 0.017]. This raises a post-hoc possibility that high EMT attenuates or reverses the MSI-high association, but it is not sufficiently decisive to support even that alternative: the interval crosses zero, exposed interaction cells are modest, and the multiplicity of interactions is large. I therefore reject H175 as written rather than convert it into a new reversal claim. Similarly, H180 is suggestive of a small PTEN-stemness interaction but remains underpowered and unresolved only as a possible signal, not as a claim. I close it as unsupported for this pre-specified interaction.\n\nOverall, I reject all ten claimed context interactions as unsupported in this dataset. This is failure to detect decisive modification, not proof of exact absence. The best current summary remains the additive association pattern: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are associated with weaker dependency, while SMARCA4 loss, MSI-high, and PTEN loss are associated with stronger dependency, with PTEN's effect smaller than the major loss effects.",
  "research_notes": "Current evidence after H172-H180: The accepted additive supplied-dataset association model is further reinforced. TP53 and KEAP1 weaker-dependency associations remain large and precise in higher mutation burden (R167, R168), adding to broad robustness across library, batch, subtype, screen quality, Cas9 activity, aneuploidy, hypoxia, and EMT main-effect strata. SMARCA4 and MSI-high stronger-dependency associations have prior discovery and validation support; PTEN is a smaller but repeated stronger-dependency signal, with several validated clean-stratum estimates. H50 PTEN in adenocarcinoma is supportive but lower bound below threshold; close as unresolved.\n\nContext-interaction search is now largely exhausted. Formal high-EMT and high-stemness interactions (H172-H180) are rejected as unsupported. H175 has an opposite-direction point but a wide interval crossing zero; do not turn it into a reversal claim without new, better-powered, preregistered evidence. No further independent validation is available.\n\nNext analyses should not chase context interactions unless a pre-specified low-confounding comparison has cell counts sufficient and a prior or clean estimate pointing decisively beyond threshold. Remaining useful analyses are limited to completing high-quality main-effect/CDKN2A refinements already registered. CDKN2A remains unresolved unless a clean lower bound exceeds 0.15 in the stronger-dependency direction. Interpret all accepted claims as supplied-dataset associations, not causality or generalizable biological mechanism."
