  "narrative": "The new results mainly confirm the supplied-dataset additive association model and leave several borderline claims unresolved. In the below-median mutation-burden stratum, TP53 loss remains associated with weaker dependency: signed estimate +0.837 [0.749, 0.924]. KEAP1 loss likewise remains associated with weaker dependency: +0.836 [0.749, 0.923]. SMARCA4 loss remains associated with stronger dependency in the pre-specified direction: +0.777 [0.694, 0.860]. PTEN loss in a clean low-mutation-burden context is a smaller but decisive stronger-dependency association: +0.293 [0.189, 0.397], with the signed lower bound clearly beyond the 0.15-unit threshold. I accept H181-H184 and close them as confirmations of the main within-dataset associations rather than claims about causality or external generalizability.\n\nCDKN2A loss remains unresolved and is now closed in the genetically motivated low-9p21 contexts. The clean deep-low-9p21 contrast is +0.121 [0.033, 0.208], broad low-9p21 is +0.126 [0.041, 0.211], and deep low-9p21 alone is +0.123 [-0.013, 0.258]. None has a lower bound decisively beyond 0.15 units, and the estimates themselves are below the effect-size threshold. The intervals are compatible with a small effect and, in H187, even with no directional effect. Because many CDKN2A contexts have now clustered below threshold, I do not promote CDKN2A to an accepted meaningful association. I close these three low-9p21 claims as unresolved, while registering two final high-quality screen/Cas9 contexts as a conservative resolution check.\n\nH188 tests MYC amplification specifically among high MYC-expression cells. The signed estimate is only +0.070 [-0.050, 0.190]; it crosses zero and is well below the threshold. Given the prior global MYC-amplification null and low prior for this post-hoc conditional effect, I reject this as unsupported rather than promote a speculative conditional association. H117 tests a technical library association for Avana and is null/non-decisive: +0.053 [-0.035, 0.141]; I reject it as a meaningful association in this dataset.\n\nPTEN-loss PIK3CA contexts do not yield decisive context-specific acceptance. In PIK3CA-mutant cells, H132 is +0.394 [0.156, 0.631], with the lower bound barely beyond threshold and exposed cell count only 38. In PIK3CA wild-type cells, H189 is +0.211 [0.109, 0.313], with lower bound below threshold. The near threshold, small subgroup, multiple PTEN-context tests, and lack of decisive support for the PTEN-by-PIK3CA interaction mean that neither PIK3CA-specific claim is robust enough to accept. I close both as unresolved. H123, PTEN loss in a clean faster-proliferating context, has estimate +0.260 [0.156, 0.365], but the lower bound again just crosses threshold with a small exposed cell count; given multiplicity and the already accepted broader PTEN association, I leave it unresolved and closed rather than accept a barely thresholded subgroup claim.\n\nOverall, the strongest supported supplied-dataset model remains additive: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss associated with weaker dependency; SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high associated with stronger dependency; PTEN loss associated with a smaller but repeated stronger-dependency signal. Context modification remains unsupported. Validation budget is exhausted, so acceptance now depends on discovery signed lower bounds, effect size, cell counts, and conservative handling of multiplicity.",
  "research_notes": "Validation budget exhausted. Accepted core within-dataset associations after the latest batch: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are associated with weaker dependency; SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high are associated with stronger dependency; PTEN loss is a smaller but repeatedly supported stronger-dependency association. Lower mutation burden main-effect checks H181-H183 further confirm TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4, and H184 confirms clean low-mutation PTEN.\n\nCDKN2A loss remains the main unresolved borderline predictor. Broad, clean, low-mutation, high-quality, and low-9p21 contexts have generally produced estimates around 0.12-0.19, but lower bounds are not decisively above 0.15. Low deep 9p21 contexts have small comparator cells and do not resolve the signal. I therefore close CDKN2A low-9p21 claims as unresolved and register two final high-quality screen/Cas9 CDKN2A checks. If those fail to exceed threshold clearly, close CDKN2A as unresolved overall.\n\nMYC amplification conditional on high MYC expression is rejected as unsupported. Technical Avana-library association is rejected as null/non-decisive. PTEN PIK3CA-mutant and PIK3CA-wild-type contexts are borderline, not accepted, because lower bounds are near threshold, cells are small in mutant context, and no decisive interaction supports context specificity. PTEN clean faster-proliferation is similarly borderline. Interpret accepted claims as dataset associations, not causal mechanisms or generalizable biology."
}

