research_signature_a is a constructed assay with arbitrary units, but its nonnegative split behaves as a strong conditional effect modifier for PTEN loss in this supplied dataset. PTEN-loss stronger dependency is amplified in the high-signature context: the broad H226 interaction, clean conditional H232 interaction, clean high-signature simple PTEN contrast, broad high-signature PTEN simple contrast, and adenocarcinoma-restricted interaction are all large and threshold-clear in the claimed direction. The low-signature complements are null or subthreshold, and the clean SMARCA4 x research_signature_a specificity control is null, favoring PTEN-specific context dependence among the tested accepted markers. This is accepted as a coherent dataset-specific conditional association, not evidence that research_signature_a has a biological role, not evidence of causality, and not evidence of external biological specificity. NEGATIVE OR SUBTHRESHOLD PREDICTORS: the tested directions for research markers D, E, and F; KRAS mutation; STK11 loss; MYC amplification; MTAP loss; ARID1A loss; RB1 loss; SMAD4 loss; BRCA2 loss; NF1 loss; APC mutation; PIK3CA mutation; broad EGFR amplification; broad ERBB2 amplification; and broad BRAF V600E did not support threshold-level dependency-score differences. Several technical, demographic, and batch contrasts were also null or subthreshold, including sex, lower serum versus standard serum, batch_a versus batch_b, library-membership contrasts, humagne_cd library, and matched RNA-DNA availability. These are non-detections at the chosen threshold, not proof of biological irrelevance. INTERACTIONS: across many technical and biological contexts, the accepted main effects are not consistently modified. Interactions involving batch, screen ROC quality, Cas9 activity, lineage subtype, mutation burden, aneuploidy, hypoxia, EMT, stemness, PIK3CA status, and many co-perturbations were rejected, imprecise, subthreshold, or non-evaluable. The PTEN x research_signature_a interaction is the main exception and is supported by both broad and clean follow-up contrasts. UNRESOLVED UNCERTAINTY: CDKN2A loss is the principal unresolved predictor. Many contexts point toward stronger dependency with signed effects roughly 0.12-0.19, but lower bounds frequently fall below the 0.15 threshold, including broad TP53- and KEAP1-restricted settings, clean MSI-excluded settings, and clean all-other-marker-free settings. Given multiplicity, small cells in some contexts, and no validation capacity, CDKN2A remains plausible but not accepted. Several PTEN context-specific contrasts remain borderline or imprecise, including some aneuploidy, hypoxia, EMT, PIK3CA, batch, and conditional-signature settings; they do not overturn the broader PTEN signal but remain uncertain. Some continuous research-signature or copy-number splits were non-evaluable because exact thresholds created insufficient cells; those should be treated as untested, not negative. Most informative next analysis: external or independent validation of CDKN2A and of the PTEN x research_signature_a conditional association would be far more valuable than additional threshold mining in this supplied dataset. If additional analyses were performed, they should use prespecified quantile or tertile definitions of research_signature_a, multiplicity control, and robustness across lineage/library/screen-quality strata. Within the current dataset, the main marker findings are adequately characterized, and further CDKN2A or borderline-context hunting would likely add little while increasing false-positive risk.",
