gnature_c: TP53 +0.833 [0.695, 0.971], KEAP1 +0.777 [0.640, 0.915], SMARCA4 +0.741 [0.622, 0.861], but research_signature_c does not show threshold-supported interaction modification for TP53 +0.010 [-0.144, 0.164], KEAP1 -0.044 [-0.199, 0.112], or SMARCA4 -0.082 [-0.222, 0.058]. This failure to detect modification is not proof of absence. Negative or non-supported findings. Tested directions for research markers D, E, and F, KRAS mutation, STK11 loss, MYC amplification, MTAP loss, ARID1A loss, RB1 loss, SMAD4 loss, BRCA2 loss, NF1 loss, APC mutation, PIK3CA mutation, broad EGFR amplification, broad ERBB2 amplification, and broad BRAF V600E did not support threshold-level dependency differences. Technical and demographic contrasts were generally not meaningful in the claimed direction, including sex, lower versus standard serum, batch_a versus batch_b, library membership contrasts, humagne_cd library, and matched RNA-DNA availability. Many interactions across lineage subtype, library, batch, screen quality, Cas9 activity, mutation burden, aneuploidy, EMT, hypoxia, stemness, PIK3CA status, and co-perturbation status were rejected, subthreshold, imprecise, or null when validated. Exact copy-number and rare subgroup splits were sometimes non-evaluable because cells were under 20 observations, especially early research_signature binarizations and some copy-number interactions; these are untested rather than negative. Unresolved uncertainty. CDKN2A loss remains unresolved as a broad predictor; its high research_signature_c association is accepted only as a supplied-dataset conditional finding and remains unvalidated. PTEN loss broad replication is clear in marker-clean settings, but several context contrasts remain uncertain, including batch_a, KY library, PIK3CA, aneuploidy, hypoxia, EMT, screen-quality, Cas9, and conditional-signature settings. The research signature modifiers are constructed standardized assays with data-dependent split choices, and unmeasured correla