ciation: broad discovery +0.239 [0.145, 0.332] and validation +0.279 [0.138, 0.419], clean TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-excluded discovery +0.252 [0.169, 0.335] with validation +0.281 [0.159, 0.403], clean MSI-excluded discovery +0.260 [0.182, 0.338] with validation +0.275 [0.154, 0.397], and clean adenocarcinoma discovery +0.279 [0.186, 0.373] with validation +0.289 [0.158, 0.420]. The PTEN broad lower bounds are sometimes near or slightly below the 0.15 threshold, but the replicated marker-clean settings support a real supplied-dataset association.\n\nSupported dataset-specific conditional associations. PTEN loss shows a coherent amplified stronger-dependency association in positive or higher research_signature_a contexts: broad research_signature_a ge 0 +0.546 [0.408, 0.684], clean +0.656 [0.542, 0.771], interaction +0.575 [0.400, 0.750], clean interaction +0.658 [0.533, 0.783], adenocarcinoma-restricted interaction +0.482 [0.277, 0.687], clean adenocarcinoma simple +0.726 [0.594, 0.858], clean adenocarcinoma interaction +0.722 [0.579, 0.864], top-quartile simple +0.546 [0.350, 0.743], top-quartile interaction +0.407 [0.186, 0.628], upper-half below top quartile +0.545 [0.346, 0.743], and clean upper-half context +0.646 [0.496, 0.795]. The complementary low or nonpositive research_signature_a PTEN contrasts are null or subthreshold, and tested specificity interactions for other accepted markers in the same context are not threshold-supported. This supports PTEN-specific conditional behavior among the tested predictors, but only as a constructed, unvalidated supplied-dataset association.\n\nCDKN2A loss is not supported as a broad predictor because broad and many restricted estimates are near, below, or imprecisely above the 0.15 threshold. However, CDKN2A loss has a coherent stronger-dependency association in upper research_signature_c contexts: upper-half simple +0.302 [0.189, 0.415], clean upper-half +0.310 [0.210, 0.410], adenocarcinoma upper-half +0.302 [0.175, 0.430], top-quartile simple +0.444 [0.294, 0.594], top-quartile interaction +0.402 [0.231, 0.572], clean top-quartile simple +0.478 [0.349, 0.606], clean interaction +0.437 [0.301, 0.572], adenocarcinoma top-quartile simple +0.402 [0.232, 0.573], clean adenocarcinoma simple +0.449 [0.296, 0.602], and clean adenocarcinoma interaction +0.398 [0.237, 0.559]. The low research_signature_c control is null and subthreshold. This supports a high-context gradient rather than a broad CDKN2A effect, but the cutoffs are analytic and constructed, and these conditional findings remain unvalidated.\n\nNegative or non-supported findings. Research markers D, E, and F, KRAS mutation, STK11 loss, MYC amplification, MTAP loss, ARID1A loss, RB1 loss, SMAD4 loss, BRCA2 loss, NF1 loss, APC mutation, PIK3CA mutation, broad EGFR amplification, broad ERBB2 amplification, and broad BRAF V600E did not support threshold-level dependency differences in the tested directions. Technical and demographic contrasts were generally not meaningful in the claimed direction, including sex, lower versus standard serum, batch_a versus batch_b, library membership contrasts, humagne_cd library, and matched RNA-DNA availability. Many interactions across lineage subtype, library, batch, screen quality, Cas9 activity, mutation burden, aneuploidy, EMT, hypoxia, stemness, PIK3CA status, and co-perturbation status were rejected, subthreshold, imprecise, or null when validated. Specificity interactions for accepted broad markers in tested signature strata were generally not threshold-supported. Failure to detect modification is not proof that modification is absent.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. CDKN2A loss remains unresolved as a broad predictor, and its high research_signature_c association remains dataset-specific and constructed. PTEN loss is replicated broadly in marker-clean settings, but many individual PTEN context contrasts remain uncertain because their intervals cross or nearly cross the threshold. The research signature modifiers are standardized constructed assays without assigned pathway or causal roles; data-dependent split choices, co-occurring mutations, library, batch, Cas9 activity, screen quality, and other correlated features may still contribute. Exact copy-number and rare subgroup splits were sometimes non-evaluable due cells under 20, so these are untested rather than negative. None of the associations establishes causality or external generalizability.\n\nMost informative next analysis. If external or independent validation becomes available, prespecify validation of PTEN-loss stronger dependency in positive or high research_signature_a contexts and CDKN2A-loss stronger dependency in high research_signature_c contexts. Validation should predefine quartile or tertile definitions, adjust for library, batch, Cas9 activity, screen ROC quality, lineage, and co-occurring accepted markers, test both simple conditional effects and interactions with multiplicity control, and evaluate complementary perturbation or phenotypic endpoints. If only this dataset remains available, the next best step is stability assessment using bootstrapping or cross-validated penalized interaction models rather than further threshold mining. No new discovery proposals are registered here.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis after validation exhaustion. No new validation was delivered and no response deadlines were active. Remaining deferred or unresolved investigations were closed without acceptance to stop further threshold mining. Accepted broad associations: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss with weaker dependency; SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high with stronger dependency; PTEN loss with smaller replicated stronger dependency in marker-clean settings. Accepted dataset-specific conditional associations: PTEN-loss stronger dependency amplified in positive/high research_signature_a contexts, and CDKN2A-loss stronger dependency only in high research_signature_c contexts. CDKN2A remains unresolved as a broad predictor. Negative findings include broad constructed markers D/E/F and most mutations/copy-number events, technical factors, demographic factors, and many interactions. Conditional signature findings are observational, constructed, unvalidated, and do not establish causality or generalizability. Most informative future work is prespecified external validation with adjustment and multiplicity control, or if restricted to this dataset, bootstrap/cross-validated model stability rather than new subgroup mining."
}

