  "narrative": "No validation capacity remains, so these final comparisons are supplied-dataset specificity and stability checks, not independent validation. They focus on the only conditional patterns that reached threshold: PTEN loss in positive/high research_signature_a and CDKN2A loss in high research_signature_c. First, I test PTEN loss after excluding TP53, KEAP1, SMARCA4, MSI-high, and CDKN2A losses in the top quartile of research_signature_a, both as an absolute conditional effect and as an interaction against the complement within marker-clean cells. This asks whether the PTEN association is not simply a consequence of co-occurring accepted markers and whether it persists in the high-signature stratum. Second, I test PTEN marker-clean cells with research_signature_a nonnegative but research_signature_c nonpositive versus research_signature_c nonnegative, probing whether the PTEN pattern is signature_a specific rather than driven by research_signature_c positivity. Third, I split CDKN2A marker-clean top-quartile research_signature_c cells by whether research_signature_a is nonpositive or nonnegative, and test an intermediate research_signature_c range, to assess whether the CDKN2A effect is a true high-signature gradient or depends on signature_a. Fourth, I test PTEN loss among CDKN2A-loss cells as a co-loss robustness check. For all negative-direction claims, a meaningful supplied-dataset association requires signed point estimate and 95% lower bound above +0.15 composite units. If cells fail or lower bounds cross the threshold, conclusions remain unresolved. These estimates are observational and do not establish causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Final accepted supplied-dataset claims remain: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are associated with weaker composite dependency; SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high are associated with stronger composite dependency; PTEN loss has a smaller but replicated stronger-dependency association, amplified in positive/high research_signature_a contexts; CDKN2A loss is not a robust broad predictor but shows dataset-specific stronger dependency in high research_signature_c contexts. Negative or nonsupported broad contrasts include research markers D/E/F, KRAS, STK11, MYC amplification, MTAP, ARID1A, RB1, SMAD4, BRCA2, NF1, APC, PIK3CA, broad EGFR/ERBB2/BRAF, and technical/demographic contrasts. Current final checks target internal specificity and stability: PTEN marker-clean top-quartile research_signature_a simple and interaction effects; PTEN marker-clean positive research_signature_a with positive versus nonpositive research_signature_c; CDKN2A marker-clean top-quartile research_signature_c split by research_signature_a; CDKN2A marker-clean intermediate research_signature_c; and PTEN effect among CDKN2A-loss. These are not external validation and do not adjust fully for all correlated technical or biological confounders. Decision rule: for negative-direction claims, accept only if signed point estimate and lower bound exceed +0.15 composite dependency-score units; otherwise unresolved or reject according to interval direction and threshold."
}

